  "notes": [
    "json is the input in export format; it goes through nodeFromJSON(json) and hash is node.hash().",
    "canonical is the exact string passed to sha1() for the top-level node (captured by hooking sha1); \"\" means no sha1 call (empty node, hash \"\").",
    "jsonText, when present, is the exact JSON text of the input when JSON.stringify cannot express it (negative zero).",
    "Child hashes are hashed recursively; children with an empty hash (null / empty objects) are skipped.",
    "ieee754 compares the SDK's doubleToIEEE754String (used for every number in a hash) with the true IEEE-754 big-endian hex. They differ in two classes: (1) |v| < 2^-971 with a normal exponent: Math.pow(2, 52 - ln) overflows to Infinity and the mantissa bits come out as 0 (random scan: 5240 of 199733 pseudo-random finite doubles differ, all with unbiased exponent in [-1022, -972]); (2) values at or next to a power of two, where floor(log(v)/LN2) is off by one (scan of 2^k, its predecessor and successor: 2299 of 6294 differ, e.g. 2^53-1 = 9007199254740991, 2^-29, 3.9999999999999996). The list contains fixed values plus every scan mismatch with k in [-60, 64]. A server that must produce the same hashes as JS clients has to reproduce this algorithm, not the true bits."
  ],
